      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "you should join the team and agree on the team's domain."
      ],
      "justification": "Implicitly starts the process and captures the initial team setup step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once that is done, create a process model and check it."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly models creating and checking the process model."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the process model is \"NOT OK\", then assign negative points."
      ],
      "justification": "Conditional step modeled as an action; preserves behaviour per relaxed guidelines."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is still \"NOT OK\", assign negative points again."
      ],
      "justification": "Handles repeated failure case correctly."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the process is okay, you can continue with it."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive outcome path preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are any issues, fix them in the next session and extend the process to levels 2 and 3."
      ],
      "justification": "Issue resolution and extension step captured accurately."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you need to check the process and assign points, continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Continuation step matches source logic."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you need to analyze the field of study, assign roles in the team."
      ],
      "justification": "Role assignment conditional step captured."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the process is okay, continue with the process and perform work according to your assigned role."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural convergence and subsequent work-performing step align with source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Check the progress and consult any problems that arise."
      ],
      "justification": "Progress monitoring step matches source exactly."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the project is accepted, present it. If not, continue working according to your role."
      ],
      "justification": "First acceptance check captured as an action node; behaviour preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b11->i12",
        "guard:b11->c9",
        "action:i12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the project is accepted, present it again. If not, continue working according to your role."
      ],
      "justification": "Second acceptance check correctly decomposed into a branch, guards extracting accepted/not-accepted states, and the presentation action. Decision logic is preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:i13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, present the project and the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Final presentation and process termination match source exactly."
    }
